
In this stage of TryHackMe, I expanded my knowledge of the Windows operating system, exploring its structure, administrative tools,
and features used to manage users and permissions.

Throughout the activities, I explored different Windows editions, the graphical user interface (GUI), the Start Menu, Taskbar, and Notification Area. 
I also learned how to navigate the file system, understand the purpose of the `C:\Windows` and `System32` folders, 
and recognize the importance of environment variables such as `%windir%`.

Another important topic was user and permission management. I worked with local accounts, groups, user profiles, and access levels,
while also understanding how User Account Control (UAC) helps protect the system against unauthorized changes.

I also explored the Control Panel and Windows settings, learning about different system configuration and management options. 
Finally, I worked with Task Manager to better understand process and resource management, including its main features and keyboard shortcuts.

This stage helped me become more familiar with the Windows environment and understand how its administrative tools and security mechanisms work.
These are important foundations for future activities involving system administration, security analysis, and Active Directory.
